  "semantic_model": {
    "conductor_eligibility": "An explicit MultiTileEntityWireElectric.addElectricWires invocation is the direct GT6 electric-conductor signal. ITEMGENERATOR.WIRES and wire/cable OreDict registrations are form/compatibility evidence and are not electrical eligibility by themselves.",
    "specification": "addElectricWires registers wireGt01..wireGt16 for every invocation and cableGt01/cableGt02/cableGt04/cableGt08/cableGt12 only when aCable is true.",
    "voltage": "The invocation's aVoltage is copied unchanged to every generated wire/cable specification as NBT_PIPESIZE and read as mVoltage.",
    "amperage": "The invocation's aAmperage is the one-conductor packet limit. NBT_PIPEBANDWIDTH and mAmperage equal aAmperage multiplied by the wire/cable gauge.",
    "loss": "GT6 defines integral EU loss per traversed wire/cable block through aLossWire/aLossCable, NBT_PIPELOSS, and mLoss. It does not define physical resistance in the material dump or in addElectricWires.",
    "insulation": "Generated cable specifications use ANY.Rubber insulation. At this revision ANY.Rubber directly re-registers MT.Rubber.",
    "traversal": "GT6 forwards depth-first in stable side order, excludes the ingress side, and uses one visited set per injection. A cable first subtracts its own loss, then greedily offers the remaining amperage to connected neighbors.",
    "overload": "A cable records only amperage used by downstream. It checks the post-loss voltage and this tick's accumulated amperage after forwarding. On overload it increments mBurnCounter and reports the full offered amperage upstream, dissipating any offered-but-undelivered energy.",
    "burn_state": "mBurnCounter reaches fire at 16 and decays on the global 512-tick phase. GT6 does not serialize mBurnCounter; CrucibleCraft intentionally persists the counter and decay phase to prevent chunk-unload reset exploits.",
    "contact_damage_runtime": "An exposed conductor with contact damage applies electricity damage from the previous tick's transferred wattage. GT6 damage is tierMax(wattage) * 4 using CS.V[].",
    "dump_gap": "The pinned OreDict material dump exposes electricalBySpecification but every row is empty because the authoritative values are supplied by loader registrations, not OreDictMaterial scalar fields."
  },
